189
00:15:22,437 --> 00:15:25,867
that was preached by Syedina Eesa(سيدناعيسى), Jesus عليه السّلام,

190
00:15:26,877 --> 00:15:32,369
believing in the oneness of Allah, believing that Eesa(عيسى) is as a messenger of Allah, rather than being the son of God.

191
00:15:32,656 --> 00:15:36,646
These were concepts that were retained by some of the Christians around the world.

192
00:15:37,227 --> 00:15:40,967
One of these men made it into Yemen,

193
00:15:41,587 --> 00:15:44,377
and started preaching in the area of Najraan(نجران).

194
00:15:45,087 --> 00:15:49,617
And their religion was spreading but secretly and privately and slowly.

195
00:15:50,477 --> 00:15:52,887
By that time Tabbana Sa'ad(تَبَّانَه سَعْدْ) was dead.

196
00:15:53,017 --> 00:15:57,557
And the king of Yemen was his son, Abu Nawaas(ابو نواس) or Du Nawaas(ذو نواس).

197
00:15:58,977 --> 00:16:06,932
News of this new religion reached to the king, and he banned it, and he persecuted the followers.

198
00:16:07,837 --> 00:16:12,857
There is the story in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم) of the king, and the young boy.

199
00:16:14,077 --> 00:16:20,661
Many scholars would attribute this story to the events between Du Nawwas(ذو نواس) and the Christians in Yemen,

200
00:16:20,955 --> 00:16:22,945
it would say that the king was Du Nawwas(ذو نواس),

201
00:16:23,674 --> 00:16:26,106
and that story is in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم) we will go over it.

202
00:16:26,727 --> 00:16:30,697
It says that the king used to deal in magic.

203
00:16:31,107 --> 00:16:33,847
And he had the sorcerer as his advisor.

204
00:16:34,937 --> 00:16:39,257
So, this sorcerer was growing old in age,

205
00:16:40,247 --> 00:16:48,464
and he told the king that I might pass away in any moment so I need to train someone, to take my place.

206
00:16:49,167 --> 00:16:53,097
 I need to inherit my skills to someone, who would carry on.

207
00:16:54,127 --> 00:17:00,430
So, they tried to find the very bright and intelligent young man and they handpicked a young man

208
00:17:00,470 --> 00:17:04,659
and they assigned him as an apprentice with this sorcerer.

209
00:17:05,363 --> 00:17:10,305
So, he was supposed to leave very early on, in the morning

210
00:17:10,389 --> 00:17:16,338
from his house and go and study under the sorcerer, and then come back home at night.

211
00:17:16,897 --> 00:17:26,373
Now this young man on his way towards the Saahir(ساحر), the sorcerer, saw a worship place.

212
00:17:27,977 --> 00:17:32,619
And he heard prayers coming in from this place, which were different.

213
00:17:33,688 --> 00:17:35,477
So, he decided to go and visit.

214
00:17:36,777 --> 00:17:44,654
And it was a church of Tauheed(توحيد) of unity of Allah, preaching the true religion of Eesa عليه السلام.

215
00:17:46,505 --> 00:17:48,875
And he was very impressed by what he was hearing.

216
00:17:49,995 --> 00:17:52,955
But he's supposed to be studying with the sorcerer.

217
00:17:53,955 --> 00:17:56,795
So, he asked the priest, he told him: What can I do?

218
00:17:57,015 --> 00:18:03,505
The priests told him, when you leave home visit me and come and study with me

219
00:18:04,095 --> 00:18:07,572
and then go to the sorcerer and if he tells you how come you were late.

220
00:18:07,629 --> 00:18:11,033
Tell him, because my parents delayed me.

221
00:18:12,365 --> 00:18:14,133
On your way back visit me.

222
00:18:14,838 --> 00:18:21,208
And when you get home, when your parents tell you how come you're late tell them that the sorcerer delayed me.

223
00:18:21,775 --> 00:18:25,428
So, you could take a class in the morning and take a class at evening.

224
00:18:25,915 --> 00:18:27,705
So, he continued doing that for a while.

225
00:18:29,175 --> 00:18:31,665
One day in the market place.

226
00:18:32,145 --> 00:18:41,481
Certain beasts entered into the market place and cause chaos, among the people and no one was able to deal with it.

227
00:18:42,295 --> 00:18:46,245
So, this young man said:

228
00:18:46,375 --> 00:18:55,597
O Allah, today I want to know whether the path of the priest or the path of the sorcerer is the truth.

229
00:18:56,425 --> 00:18:58,435
So, O Allah, show me the truth.

230
00:18:59,355 --> 00:19:04,432
And everyone was attempting to kill this beast and no one succeeded.

231
00:19:05,255 --> 00:19:08,151
And then this boy picked up a rock and he said:

232
00:19:08,197 --> 00:19:13,137
O Allah! If the path of the priest is the truth, then kill this animal.

233
00:19:13,585 --> 00:19:17,165
And he threw the rock, and it killed the animal immediately.

234
00:19:18,966 --> 00:19:21,994
He went back and reported this to the priest, he told him what happened.!

235
00:19:22,029 --> 00:19:27,620
The priest told him, my son, today you have achieved, attained a very high status.

236
00:19:27,866 --> 00:19:30,136
Therefore, you would be tested,

237
00:19:31,308 --> 00:19:33,228
you will go through trials,

238
00:19:33,748 --> 00:19:38,368
no one can reach such a high status without being tested by Allah.

239
00:19:40,638 --> 00:19:46,467
In exams, the better the student, the more difficult the exam should be.

240
00:19:47,478 --> 00:19:51,601
Because you want to tell the difference between the levels of the students.

241
00:19:51,708 --> 00:19:56,346
So, you have easy questions, which everyone is able to answer.

242
00:19:56,918 --> 00:20:00,208
And then you have medium difficulty.

243
00:20:00,638 --> 00:20:03,418
And then you have difficult and then you have very difficult,

244
00:20:03,658 --> 00:20:06,673
because you want to distinguish the A plus, from A minus.

245
00:20:06,844 --> 00:20:08,226
You want to tell the difference.

246
00:20:08,668 --> 00:20:12,962
Same thing Allahسبحانه وتعالى has brought us on this earth for a test.

247
00:20:13,808 --> 00:20:16,188
And according to your level, you would be tested.

248
00:20:16,528 --> 00:20:17,872
Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

249
00:20:17,912 --> 00:20:21,482
اَشَدِّالنَّاسْ بَلَادْ اَلْاَنْبِيَآءْ، فَالْاَمْثَلْ فَالْاَمْثَلْ

250
00:20:21,818 --> 00:20:24,821
The ones, who go through the most difficult tests are the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

251
00:20:25,988 --> 00:20:28,188
And then it goes down according to your level.

252
00:20:29,168 --> 00:20:34,627
So, this priest was telling the young man, you will be tested.

253
00:20:35,058 --> 00:20:41,629
And then he told him and when you are tested, do not disclose my name.

254
00:20:43,338 --> 00:20:45,628
Because the priest was doing his Da'wah(دعوة) in secret.

255
00:20:46,598 --> 00:20:49,618
And he doesn't want his name to be exposed.

256
00:20:50,008 --> 00:20:54,648
It is not out of fear, this is for the security of the Da'wah(دعوة).

257
00:20:55,478 --> 00:21:01,768
So, he told him, and when you go through trials, do not mention my name.

258
00:21:04,288 --> 00:21:09,211
And down the road, we’ll see that the priest was a very courageous man.

259
00:21:09,281 --> 00:21:11,975
 I mean, he might wonder, why is he saying don't mention my name?

260
00:21:12,015 --> 00:21:12,803
What is he afraid of?

261
00:21:12,865 --> 00:21:15,010
How come he can't just go outside and say:

262
00:21:15,228 --> 00:21:17,644
Here I'm a Muslim and invite everybody openly?

263
00:21:17,828 --> 00:21:19,794
Why is he afraid, why is he keeping a secret?

264
00:21:20,032 --> 00:21:24,311
But you will see that the priests was a very courageous man, but he was a wise man too.

265
00:21:25,008 --> 00:21:29,228
The Associate of the king was blind.

266
00:21:29,638 --> 00:21:37,114
And he came to this young man to cure him because now the young man has studied under the sorcerer.

267
00:21:37,618 --> 00:21:39,998
So, now he is the expert people go to him.

268
00:21:41,248 --> 00:21:44,218
So, when he went to the young man, the young man told him;

269
00:21:44,418 --> 00:21:48,698
I cannot heal you, but Allah can heal you, Allah can do it,

270
00:21:50,078 --> 00:21:52,630
and he healed the man.

271
00:21:53,208 --> 00:21:59,958
So, the blind man who's now cured, went to the king, and the king told him; Who cured you.?

272
00:22:00,268 --> 00:22:01,292
The man said: Allah.

273
00:22:01,770 --> 00:22:05,223
The king said and do you have a god other than me?

274
00:22:06,448 --> 00:22:09,368
The man said: Yes, Allah is my Lord and your Lord.

275
00:22:09,908 --> 00:22:14,138
The king tortured, this friend of his,

276
00:22:14,528 --> 00:22:18,316
and told him to disclose the name of the person, who taught him this.

277
00:22:19,818 --> 00:22:29,012
And under the persecution, he gave up the name and said it is the young man or the boy.

278
00:22:30,488 --> 00:22:34,468
Now, they brought in the boy, and they started to torture him.

279
00:22:36,218 --> 00:22:44,118
And the boy under duress, and pain did give up the name of his teacher, the priest.

280
00:22:45,948 --> 00:22:51,458
He could not sustain the pain and suffering that he was going through, so he disclosed the name

281
00:22:52,578 --> 00:22:57,198
So, now they brought the priest and they told the priest, to give up his religion.

282
00:22:57,698 --> 00:22:58,778
And he refused.

283
00:22:59,798 --> 00:23:06,786
So, they brought a saw, and they place it on top of his head, and they cut him into two.

284
00:23:07,858 --> 00:23:10,108
 But he refused to give up his religion.

285
00:23:11,494 --> 00:23:16,204
This is the courage that he had and this is the perseverance and the patience.

286
00:23:16,584 --> 00:23:19,794
He gave up his life, he was tortured brutally.

287
00:23:20,104 --> 00:23:21,514
But he never gave up his religion.

288
00:23:22,664 --> 00:23:25,157
And now they're left with the boy.

289
00:23:25,654 --> 00:23:32,109
So, the king ordered a group of his soldiers to carry this boy and throw him from the top of a cliff.

290
00:23:33,434 --> 00:23:34,531
They carried the boy

291
00:23:34,986 --> 00:23:40,784
and Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), Allah was performing Karamaat(كرامات) on the hand of this boy.

292
00:23:41,174 --> 00:23:43,894
Karamah(كرامة) is a miracle that would occur to a Non-Prophet.

293
00:23:45,209 --> 00:23:46,848
And miracles happen to the Prophets.

294
00:23:47,125 --> 00:23:49,185
That's the difference between Mujizza(معجزه) and Karamah(كرامة).

295
00:23:50,184 --> 00:23:55,972
Mu'jizah(معجزة) happens to a Prophet and Karama(كرامه) happens to a person, who is not a Prophet,

296
00:23:56,214 --> 00:23:58,604
but they are both supernatural events.

297
00:23:59,594 --> 00:24:03,504
So, this boy made Dua(دُعَا) to Allah and said: O Allah

298
00:24:03,624 --> 00:24:04,473
اِكْفِنِيْهِمْ بِمَا شِئْتْ

299
00:24:04,559 --> 00:24:06,842
O Allah take care of them, the way you want,

300
00:24:07,204 --> 00:24:08,454
I'm going to leave it, up to you

301
00:24:08,784 --> 00:24:11,634
O Allah take care of them the way you want.

302
00:24:12,254 --> 00:24:18,305
Allahسبحانه وتعالى made them reach, the top of the cliff, and then the cliff started to shake.

303
00:24:18,681 --> 00:24:21,868
And all of the soldiers fell down, except he.

304
00:24:22,954 --> 00:24:26,044
And now the boy is walking back and he entered into the palace of the king,

305
00:24:26,085 --> 00:24:27,075
here I am again.

306
00:24:27,674 --> 00:24:34,254
So, the king appointed another group of soldiers to take him, obviously soldiers are disposable with this king.

307
00:24:34,411 --> 00:24:38,752
So, he appointed, the new group of soldiers to take him into a ship.

308
00:24:39,084 --> 00:24:43,634
And when they reach into the deep waters, just throw him in the water.

309
00:24:44,284 --> 00:24:47,556
So, they were on this boat, and he made the same Dua(دعا) again,

310
00:24:47,615 --> 00:24:49,545
O Allah take care of them the way you want to.

311
00:24:50,654 --> 00:24:54,789
The boat capsized, and they all drowned, except he,

312
00:24:55,784 --> 00:24:57,624
he went back to safety.

313
00:24:59,054 --> 00:25:03,825
So, he went to the king, and the king was ready to appoint a third group of soldiers to take him.

314
00:25:04,174 --> 00:25:05,494
The boy told him wait,

315
00:25:05,854 --> 00:25:11,201
you're not going to be able to kill me, unless you do what I tell you.

316
00:25:12,724 --> 00:25:14,634
The King told him, what is it.?

317
00:25:15,624 --> 00:25:21,184
The boy said, you tie me to a tree and you gather everyone

318
00:25:21,754 --> 00:25:24,356
and you bring an arrow and you say: Bismillah(بسم الله),

319
00:25:24,844 --> 00:25:26,494
the Lord of the boy,

320
00:25:27,434 --> 00:25:29,024
then you will be able to kill me.

321
00:25:30,316 --> 00:25:34,594
So, the boy told him the prescription of how to kill him.

322
00:25:35,984 --> 00:25:46,600
And this is one of the many evidences given, for the justification of what is referred to as suicide bombings.

323
00:25:47,394 --> 00:25:51,132
These are one of the evidences that are given that it is allowed.

324
00:25:51,524 --> 00:25:54,824
Obviously there are restrictions on when it is allowed and where.

325
00:25:55,134 --> 00:26:01,348
But the concept itself of a person giving up their life for Allahسبحانه وتعالى is a valid one,

326
00:26:01,734 --> 00:26:03,644
based on this evidence, and many others.

327
00:26:05,234 --> 00:26:11,010
Because he told the king, how it is possible to get rid of him.

