00:30:57,572 --> 00:31:02,842
and Ar-Rayyat(أرياط) invaded Yemen, and fought with Du Nawaas(ذو نواس),

398
00:31:03,702 --> 00:31:07,032
and Du Nawaas(ذو نواس), when he lost, he committed suicide.

399
00:31:07,332 --> 00:31:12,170
It says that he was on his horse, and he just jumped in, to the Red Sea, he killed himself.

400
00:31:12,432 --> 00:31:18,045
 So, he lost, and now the Abyssinians were ruling over parts of Yemen.

401
00:31:18,244 --> 00:31:24,355
And they did this as a revenge for the Christians, who were killed by the Jews of Yemen.

402
00:31:25,832 --> 00:31:30,382
Ar-Rayyat(أرياط) ruled over Yemen for a while, he was very strict.

403
00:31:31,372 --> 00:31:37,784
One of his army generals staged a revolt against him,

404
00:31:38,632 --> 00:31:43,562
and the Abyssinians in Yemen, were divided now,

405
00:31:44,152 --> 00:31:46,143
a group of them were with Ar-Rayyat(أرياط),

406
00:31:46,592 --> 00:31:50,734
and the other group were with the new leader called Abraha(أبرهة).

407
00:31:52,432 --> 00:31:53,482
And they were fighting,

408
00:31:55,312 --> 00:32:02,332
Ar-Rayyat(أرياط) told Abraha(أبرهة); If we kill each other, the people of the land will take over.

409
00:32:03,112 --> 00:32:08,595
So, how about we have a one-on-one fight, a man to man, Me and You.

410
00:32:09,612 --> 00:32:11,302
Abraha(أبرهة) agreed.

411
00:32:12,182 --> 00:32:18,402
But Abraha(أبرهة) made a secret agreement with some of his security guards.

412
00:32:19,292 --> 00:32:23,472
That if you see me losing, jump in and help,

413
00:32:24,902 --> 00:32:26,528
if you see me winning, leave me alone.

414
00:32:26,986 --> 00:32:29,320
If you see that I'm losing come in.

415
00:32:30,802 --> 00:32:36,882
So, you have all these people surrounding and Abraha(أبرهة) and Ar-Rayyat(أرياط) are in the middle,

416
00:32:37,752 --> 00:32:41,115
now Ar-Rayyat(أرياط) was described as a tall and thin man,

417
00:32:41,462 --> 00:32:44,009
and Abraha(أبرهة) was short and chubby.

418
00:32:45,352 --> 00:32:51,829
So, Ar-Rayyat(أرياط) he was able to strike Abraha(أبرهة) from the top and he chopped off his nose.

419
00:32:52,922 --> 00:32:55,375
So, Abraha(أبرهة) was called Abraha Al-Ushrum (أبرهة ألأشرم),

420
00:32:55,420 --> 00:32:57,450
Ashram(اشرم), means his nose is chopped off.

421
00:32:58,762 --> 00:33:04,471
When that happened, the bodyguards jumped in and they killed Ar-Rayyat(أرياط).

422
00:33:06,722 --> 00:33:09,199
He betrayed obviously this is against rules,

423
00:33:09,452 --> 00:33:12,225
but the issue is over now, Ar-Rayyat(أرياط) is dead.

424
00:33:14,222 --> 00:33:19,182
Abraha(أبرهة) now took over and he was the one, ruling over Yemen.

425
00:33:20,232 --> 00:33:26,222
Abraha(أبرهة) wanted to change the religion of the people,

426
00:33:26,682 --> 00:33:29,302
and forced them to become Christian.

427
00:33:30,682 --> 00:33:33,782
And since the Arabs were attached to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

428
00:33:34,572 --> 00:33:40,952
he decided to build a counterpart to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) in Sana'a(صنعاء), in Yemen.

429
00:33:42,402 --> 00:33:46,352
So, he built a huge Cathedral called Al-Kulais(ألكليس).

430
00:33:47,052 --> 00:33:52,552
And this was described as a wonderful piece of art and huge, and great.

431
00:33:52,786 --> 00:33:55,957
I mean, he had access of wealth from Abyssinia.

432
00:33:55,996 --> 00:34:00,646
So, they built this huge Cathedral in Sana'a(صنعاء) to compete with Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

433
00:34:01,652 --> 00:34:06,842
Now, one man didn't like this idea.

434
00:34:07,472 --> 00:34:09,695
What he did was a bit crude.

435
00:34:10,366 --> 00:34:14,654
 He went into Al-Kullais(ألكليس), and he defecated

436
00:34:15,125 --> 00:34:19,028
and then not only that, he took it and he spread it all over the walls

437
00:34:20,042 --> 00:34:24,258
stool, imagine stool all over the walls, and he ran away.

438
00:34:25,222 --> 00:34:26,641
Abraha(أبرهة) was furious.

439
00:34:26,803 --> 00:34:29,002
What is this, what is this guy doing?

440
00:34:30,722 --> 00:34:34,582
He was so angry, he decided that he must get rid of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

441
00:34:35,262 --> 00:34:37,712
I mean, I'm going to put an end to this, and destroy Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

442
00:34:38,252 --> 00:34:41,182
he mobilized an army and the march towards Makkah.

443
00:34:42,302 --> 00:34:46,424
There was some resistance along the way, one of the chiefs of a tribe,

444
00:34:46,772 --> 00:34:48,598
his name is Nufail(نفيل).

445
00:34:49,002 --> 00:34:51,907
He put up some resistance, but he was defeated,

446
00:34:51,943 --> 00:34:53,901
I mean Abraha(أبرهة) is a huge powerful army.

447
00:34:54,342 --> 00:34:58,642
And they captured Nufail(نفيل), they captured him as a prisoner of war.

448
00:34:59,522 --> 00:35:01,931
When Abraha(أبرهة) reached to At-Taef(ألطائف),

449
00:35:02,054 --> 00:35:06,294
the people of At-Taef(ألطائف) assisted Abraha(أبرهة),

450
00:35:06,762 --> 00:35:12,322
and one of them offered to be a guide for Abraha(أبرهة), for the rest of the journey.

451
00:35:12,732 --> 00:35:15,192
And this man his name is Abu Raghal(أبو رغال).

452
00:35:15,722 --> 00:35:17,614
So, Abu Raghal(أبو رغال), he went out to the army.

453
00:35:17,683 --> 00:35:20,923
But then immediately when they got out of At-Taef(ألطائف) he died.

454
00:35:21,577 --> 00:35:24,325
So, then the Arabs were so upset with Abu Raghal(أبو رغال)

455
00:35:24,400 --> 00:35:30,355
they built in the place of his death a monument that they would stone, because of his betrayal.

456
00:35:31,032 --> 00:35:36,581
Anyway, Abraha(أبرهة) made it to the outskirts of Makkah

457
00:35:37,432 --> 00:35:42,642
And there were some shepherds with camels, grazing

458
00:35:43,932 --> 00:35:45,532
He took possession of them.

459
00:35:46,508 --> 00:35:51,474
200 of these camels belonged to Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) the grandfather of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

460
00:35:52,655 --> 00:35:57,085
So, Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) came out of Makkah to meet with Abraha(أبرهة).

461
00:35:58,285 --> 00:36:03,675
Now obviously, Abraha(أبرهة), you can't just walk in and meet him, he was such a important figure.

462
00:36:04,165 --> 00:36:06,831
So, Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) has to have some connections to get in,

463
00:36:07,515 --> 00:36:12,045
Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) happened to be a friend of Nufail(نفيل).

464
00:36:13,045 --> 00:36:15,235
Who was captured as a prisoner of war.

465
00:36:16,295 --> 00:36:19,675
Nufail(نفيل) was carried with the army.

466
00:36:20,745 --> 00:36:26,165
And he befriended, he became friends with a man called Unais(أنيس).

467
00:36:26,585 --> 00:36:31,515
And this man Unais(أنيس) was such an important person in the army.

468
00:36:32,135 --> 00:36:38,315
He was a pilot of the elephant, which was their most valuable, piece of equipment.

469
00:36:39,205 --> 00:36:43,895
So, Nufail(نفيل) now is very well connected, he knows Unais(أنيس).

470
00:36:44,285 --> 00:36:47,631
So, Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) came to Nufail(نفيل) and told him; I want to meet with Abraha(أبرهة).

471
00:36:48,523 --> 00:36:53,288
 Nufail(نفيل) told him: Sure, I'll arrange for your a meeting through my friend Unais(أنيس).

472
00:36:54,435 --> 00:36:56,734
So, Unais(أنيس) arranged the meeting with Abraha(أبرهة).

473
00:36:57,035 --> 00:36:58,965
And Abraha(أبرهة) welcomed Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب).

474
00:37:00,465 --> 00:37:01,985
Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) walked in,

475
00:37:02,645 --> 00:37:07,076
and Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) was described as being a man with a very strong presence in all.

476
00:37:07,545 --> 00:37:11,235
I mean, by just seeing him, a person becomes impressed.

477
00:37:14,135 --> 00:37:15,835
So, when Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) came in,

478
00:37:16,545 --> 00:37:20,334
Abraha(أبرهة) held him, in a high esteem, even though they didn't even talk yet.

479
00:37:21,905 --> 00:37:26,595
Now, the rules were that Abraha(أبرهة) sits on a very high throne.

480
00:37:27,075 --> 00:37:29,095
And people sit under his feet.

481
00:37:29,625 --> 00:37:32,575
So, you come and have a meeting with Abraha(أبرهة), you are sitting under his feet.

482
00:37:33,225 --> 00:37:38,505
Abraha(أبرهة), when he saw Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب), he didn't feel comfortable at all,

483
00:37:39,335 --> 00:37:41,125
having Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) sit under him.

484
00:37:42,465 --> 00:37:46,026
But he cannot also allow Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) to sit with him,

485
00:37:46,074 --> 00:37:49,092
on the throne because nobody should sit on the throne, except he.

486
00:37:50,155 --> 00:37:53,055
So, what he did is he came down from his throne

487
00:37:53,495 --> 00:37:56,275
and sat with Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) on the floor.

488
00:37:56,965 --> 00:37:58,389
And he told Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب),

489
00:37:58,628 --> 00:38:01,705
he told the interpreter to ask Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب), what does he need?

490
00:38:02,775 --> 00:38:05,775
Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) straight ahead, told the interpreter.

491
00:38:06,695 --> 00:38:10,955
Abraha(أبرهة) has taken possession of 200 of my camels, I want them back.

492
00:38:12,745 --> 00:38:20,050
Abraha(أبرهة) responded and said: When I saw you, I had so much respect for you, but I've lost it all.

493
00:38:20,724 --> 00:38:24,355
I'm coming to destroy your honor and the honor of your father's,

494
00:38:24,535 --> 00:38:28,125
I am coming to destroy the center of your livelihood,

495
00:38:28,305 --> 00:38:32,170
I am coming to destroy Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), and you're asking me about camels.

496
00:38:33,725 --> 00:38:39,405
Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) responded and said: I am the owner of the camels.

497
00:38:40,575 --> 00:38:42,175
So, I'm responsible for them.

498
00:38:42,595 --> 00:38:47,395
And this house belongs to Allah and Allah will protect it.

499
00:38:48,775 --> 00:38:53,695
I'm here to ask for what is under my authority, my responsibility.

500
00:38:54,055 --> 00:38:57,735
The house belongs to Allah, Allah will take care of it and Allah will protect it.

501
00:38:58,695 --> 00:39:00,395
Abraha(أبرهة) said give him back his camels.

502
00:39:01,365 --> 00:39:04,995
Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) went back to Makkah and he told the people of Makkah,

503
00:39:05,385 --> 00:39:08,815
do not fight, withdraw out of Makkah,

504
00:39:09,955 --> 00:39:11,745
Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) gave them clear instructions.

505
00:39:11,809 --> 00:39:14,161
We're not going to fight Abraha(أبرهة), we're going to leave.

506
00:39:14,585 --> 00:39:17,285
And they all went up to the mountains.

507
00:39:17,645 --> 00:39:20,695
And Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) was the last one to leave and before he left,

508
00:39:21,385 --> 00:39:26,475
he was hanging on the clothes of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) or the handle of the door of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

509
00:39:27,025 --> 00:39:32,207
And he was praying to Allahسبحانه وتعالى to protect His house, and then he left.

510
00:39:33,385 --> 00:39:39,297
So, all of them have evacuated, everyone evacuated Makkah.

511
00:39:39,645 --> 00:39:43,465
And Abraha(أبرهة) now issued his instructions to march forth.

512
00:39:44,665 --> 00:39:47,365
But the elephant refused to move.

513
00:39:49,915 --> 00:39:53,165
They turned the elephant to a different direction, he would stand up running.

514
00:39:53,625 --> 00:39:57,305
They turned him towards the direction of Makkah, he would sit down.

515
00:39:58,065 --> 00:40:03,485
How come, a miracle from Allah but it is said in the story,

516
00:40:03,575 --> 00:40:09,015
that this man Nufail(نفيل), who was a prisoner of war, he released himself from his chains,

517
00:40:09,523 --> 00:40:13,721
and he jumped to the ear of the elephant and he said to the elephant,

518
00:40:13,771 --> 00:40:16,385
this is the house of Allah, do not attack it and he ran away.

519
00:40:17,155 --> 00:40:23,269
But whether that was the reason or not, the elephant refused to march in the direction of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

520
00:40:23,765 --> 00:40:27,285
and they would beat it, they started poking it with their spears,

521
00:40:27,459 --> 00:40:30,859
and the elephant was bleeding, it refused to move.

522
00:40:31,375 --> 00:40:33,675
Eventually, they decided they're gonna have to leave the elephant

523
00:40:33,895 --> 00:40:35,735
and they made their move forward.

524
00:40:36,365 --> 00:40:38,975
Allahسبحانه وتعالى sent on them an army.

525
00:40:39,505 --> 00:40:43,275
No, one knows the soldiers of Allah, anything can be a soldier of Allah.

526
00:40:43,575 --> 00:40:46,985
Water which is the source of life can be a soldier of Allah.

527
00:40:47,245 --> 00:40:50,678
Water is, what killed the tyrant, Firoun(فرعون).

528
00:40:51,420 --> 00:40:53,172
Wind is a soldier of Allah,

529
00:40:53,515 --> 00:40:55,866
وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُودَ رَبِّكَ إِلَّا هُوَ ۚ

530
00:40:55,906 --> 00:40:59,179
Allahسبحانه وتعالى says; No one knows His soldiers but He.

531
00:40:59,858 --> 00:41:02,855
So, Allahسبحانه وتعالى sent an army of birds,

532
00:41:03,385 --> 00:41:09,263
every birds carrying with it, missiles, that were sent on the army of Abraha(أبرهة)

533
00:41:09,463 --> 00:41:12,360
and destroy them all, they were all killed.

534
00:41:13,285 --> 00:41:16,695
And this event was recorded in Surat Tul Feel(سورةالفيل).

535
00:41:16,925 --> 00:41:26,718
أَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِأَصْحَابِ الْفِيلِ۝أَلَمْ يَجْعَلْ كَيْدَهُمْ فِي تَضْلِيلٍ۝

536
00:41:27,162 --> 00:41:36,574
وَأَرْسَلَ عَلَيْهِمْ طَيْرًا أَبَابِيلَ۝ تَرْمِيهِمْ بِحِجَارَةٍ مِنْ سِجِّيلٍ۝

537
00:41:37,056 --> 00:41:42,730
فَجَعَلَهُمْ كَعَصْفٍ مَأْكُولٍ۝

538
00:41:43,775 --> 00:41:51,472
These are the events up to the year, in which Rasool Allah ﷺ was born.

539
00:41:51,585 --> 00:41:55,125
Rasool Allah ﷺ was born in the year of the elephant,

540
00:41:55,965 --> 00:41:59,527
in the same year, Rasool Allah ﷺ was born.

541
00:41:59,965 --> 00:42:03,005
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

